<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment 267,000 in December - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment 267,000 in December - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of those claiming unemployment benefit fell to a seasonally adjusted 267,000 in December from 268,700 in November, the Central Statistics Office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>			    Unadjusted	    Adjusted</p>
<p> Latest		     270,146		267,000</p>
<p> Previous		 263,305		268,700</p>
<p> Year-ago		285,423		282,300</p>
<p>--Dublin newsroom 353-1-661-3377.</p>
</text>
